<title>USA: Financial Times taps Doremus for U.S. ads.</title>
<headline>Financial Times taps Doremus for U.S. ads.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Doremus Advertising, a unit of Omnicom Group Inc, said Thursday it has won the U.S. account of the newspaper The Financial Times, owned by Pearson Plc. The account, said the company, is valued at between $3 million and $6 million.</p>
<p>The company said that privately-held Bozell, Jacobs, Kenyon &amp; Eckhardt will continue to handle the global branding assignments for the The Financial Times.</p>
</text>
